  "description": "Gneedle.Inject is the weaver. It builds and rewrites the IL of .NET assemblies through Mono.Cecil, and weaves a body from a template, which is an ordinary C# method: the template reaches the members of the type it is woven into through the placeholders This, Base, Object, Static and Proceed, and names a generic parameter of that type through the tokens T_0 to T_20 and M_0 to M_20. Around advice keeps the body which the method already held and lets the template proceed into it. It is driven the same way from a code generator, from a tool of your own, or from the build task in Gneedle.Aspect.",
  "id": "Gneedle.Inject",
